From c29c7e905357c14c94a2cc5b73b5a02a404146a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leo Wilkin <leo@hackclub.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:30:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: app-scoped OAuth tokens for native clients

Native apps can ask for scope=app on /oauth/authorize. The consent page says the
app gets full access, and the bearer token then works on tRPC (including the
board.onEvent stream) and the file routes, not just /api/mcp. App tokens only go
to custom-scheme or loopback redirects, and site-admin powers stay browser-only.

